# Generated by tools/make_helper_proxies.py.
#
# No texture, and this is the slot where that shows most: real hair
# HAD no alpha-cut strand texture, because the geometry carried no UVs to
# map one onto. Both are fixed; see `diffuseTexture` below. The note read:
# "needs an alpha-cut strand texture, which the cage geometry cannot
# stand in for. This is honest placeholder shading on honest
# reference geometry, not a hair groom.
name Hair
tag MakeHuman™
ambientColor 0.04 0.03 0.02
diffuseColor 0.28 0.19 0.13
specularColor 0.6 0.6 0.6
shininess 0.3
opacity 1.0
# transparent True, and the flag is load-bearing: the eye material records
# that "without the flag the renderer discards that alpha and paints an opaque
# disc over the iris". The same applies here -- the strand texture is alpha-cut
# and without this it renders as a solid tube with a stripe pattern painted on.
transparent True
# THE STRAND TEXTURE. This file used to say a strand texture was needed and
# that the cage geometry could not stand in for one. Both halves are here now:
# the sweeps emit UVs (u around the tube, v along it) and
# tools/make_hair_alpha.py cuts the tube lengthwise into eight strands that
# thin toward the tip.
diffuseTexture ../hair_strands.png
backfaceCull True
castShadows True
receiveShadows True
shader data/shaders/glsl/litsphere
